query:
[Feature]: A CLI option to generate missing snapshots and not fail the tests because of missing snapshots

### 🚀 Feature Request

I request a CLI `--update-snapshots=missing-no-failure` option that makes Playwright write missing snapshots, but not mark the assertions with missing snapshots as failed.

This is basically a duplicate of #27217, #23502 and #31503. I open a new issue to show that the feature request is still up-to-date.

### Example

_No response_

### Motivation

My team develops on macOS and Windows, but run CI tests on Linux (namely, GitHub Actions). Therefore, snapshots produced on the developer's local machines don't match the snapshots generated in the CI. Therefore, the tests fail.

To solve that, we delegate snapshot generation to the CI. The CI pipeline runs the tests while generating the missing snapshots, and pushes the missing snapshots to the Git branch it was triggered from. The existing options for generation the missing snapshots don't work:
- `--update-snapshots` generates all snapshots, even old ones, which basically disables all snapshot assertions;
- `--update-snapshots=missing` generates only missing snapshots, but marks the tests as failed;
- splitting snapshot generation (with `--update-snapshots` and pushing only new files) and test running (with no `--update-snapshots`) into separate jobs increases the CI end-to-end execution time and resource consumption twice;
- snapshots generated in a local Playwright Docker image don't always match the CI snapshots because of [emulation bugs](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/19677).

Our current workaround is using `--update-snapshots=missing`, letting the `playwright test` fail, and checking the JSON report for actual failures using a custom script:

<details><summary>The script</summary>

```ts
import { readFileSync } from 'fs'
import path from 'path'

type PlaywrightReport = {
  errors?: PlaywrightError[]
  suites?: PlaywrightSuite[]
}

type PlaywrightError = {
  message?: string
}

type PlaywrightSuite = {
  specs?: PlaywrightSpec[]
  suites?: PlaywrightSuite[]
}

type PlaywrightSpec = {
  tests?: PlaywrightTest[]
}

type PlaywrightTest = {
  results?: PlaywrightTestResult[]
  status?: 'expected' | 'flaky' | 'skipped' | 'unexpected'
}

type PlaywrightTestResult = {
  error?: PlaywrightError
  errors?: PlaywrightError[]
}

const PLAYWRIGHT_REPORT_PATH = path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, '../report/report.json')

const WRITTEN_MISSING_SNAPSHOT_ERROR =
  /(?:^|\n)(?:Error: )?A snapshot doesn't exist at .+?, writing actual\./

function main(): number {
  let report: PlaywrightReport
  try {
    report = JSON.parse(readFileSync(PLAYWRIGHT_REPORT_PATH, 'utf8')) as PlaywrightReport
  } catch (error) {
    const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)
    console.error(`Could not read the Playwright test report: ${message}`)
    return 1
  }

  const failures = getPlaywrightFailureMessages(report)
  if (!failures.length) {
    return 0
  }

  console.error('Playwright failures:')
  for (const failure of failures) {
    console.error(`  ${failure}`)
  }
  return 1
}

function getPlaywrightFailureMessages(report: PlaywrightReport): string[] {
  const errors = [...(report.errors ?? []), ...getSuiteErrors(report.suites ?? [])]
  return errors.flatMap(getFailureMessage)
}

function getSuiteErrors(suites: PlaywrightSuite[]): PlaywrightError[] {
  return suites.flatMap((suite) => [
    ...(suite.specs?.flatMap(getSpecErrors) ?? []),
    ...getSuiteErrors(suite.suites ?? []),
  ])
}

function getSpecErrors(spec: PlaywrightSpec): PlaywrightError[] {
  return spec.tests?.flatMap(getTestErrors) ?? []
}

function getTestErrors(test: PlaywrightTest): PlaywrightError[] {
  const errors = test.results?.flatMap(getResultErrors) ?? []
  if (errors.length || test.status === 'expected' || test.status === 'skipped' || test.status === undefined) {
    return errors
  }

  return [{ message: `Playwright reported an ${test.status} test without an error message.` }]
}

function getResultErrors(result: PlaywrightTestResult): PlaywrightError[] {
  return result.errors?.length ? result.errors : result.error ? [result.error] : []
}

function getFailureMessage(error: PlaywrightError): string[] {
  if (error.message === undefined) {
    return ['Playwright reported an error without a message.']
  }

  return WRITTEN_MISSING_SNAPSHOT_ERROR.test(error.message) ? [] : [error.message]
}

process.exitCode = main()
```

</details>

Replacing this whole script with `--update-snapshots=missing-no-failure` would be such an elegant solution.

